e(43,D_PAIR+" Identify the pair(s) wherein the Passive Voice is correctly stated.","Read the following pairs:\nI. Active: These grapes taste sour. | Passive: These grapes are sour when they are tasted.\nII. Active: Forget the past. | Passive: Let the past be forgotten.",["I only","II only","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"B",*VN[:1],VN[1],"Voice","Passive of imperative and linking verb","M","Concept: 'taste sour' uses taste as a linking verb, so it has no true passive; 'are sour when they are tasted' changes the meaning.\nPair II: the passive of an imperative is 'Let + object + be + past participle', so 'Let the past be forgotten' is correct.\nAnswer: (b)") if False else None
