e2(43,D_PAIR+" Identify the pair(s) wherein the Passive Voice is correctly stated.","Read the following pairs:\nI. Active: These grapes taste sour. | Passive: These grapes are sour when they are tasted.\nII. Active: Forget the past. | Passive: Let the past be forgotten.",["I only","II only","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"B",*VOICE,"Passive of linking verb and imperative","M","Concept: 'taste sour' uses taste as a linking verb, which has no true passive; 'are sour when they are tasted' changes the meaning.\nPair II: the passive of an imperative is 'Let + object + be + past participle', so 'Let the past be forgotten' is correct.\nAnswer: (b)")
e2(44,D_PAIR+" Identify the pair(s) wherein the Passive Voice is correctly stated.","Read the following pairs:\nI. Active: They asked me my name. | Passive: My name was asked by them.\nII. Active: They found him guilty. | Passive: He found them guilty.",["I only","II only","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"A",*VOICE,"Passive with two objects","M","Pair I: with two objects, one can become the subject; 'My name was asked by them' keeps the meaning, so it is acceptable.\nPair II: 'He found them guilty' reverses the doer and the receiver, so it is not a passive of the active sentence (it should be 'He was found guilty by them').\nAnswer: (a)")
e2(45,D_PAIR+" Identify the pair(s) wherein the Indirect Speech is correctly stated.","Read the following pairs:\nI. Direct: He said, \"Bravo! You have written the best answer.\" | Indirect: He applauded him saying that he had written the best answer.\nII. Direct: \"The sun rises in the East,\" said the teacher. | Indirect: The teacher said that the sun rose in the East.",["I only","II only","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"A",*NARR,"Reporting exclamations and universal truths","M","Pair I: 'Bravo!' becomes 'applauded', and the present perfect becomes past perfect: correct.\nPair II: a universal truth keeps the present tense ('the sun rises'), so changing it to 'rose' is wrong.\nAnswer: (a)")
e2(46,D_PAIR+" Identify the pair(s) wherein the Indirect Speech is correctly stated.","Read the following pairs:\nI. Direct: He said to him, \"Wait here until I return.\" | Indirect: He ordered him to wait here until he returned.\nII. Direct: He said, \"Alas! I am undone.\" | Indirect: He exclaimed sadly that he was undone.",["I only","II only","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"B",*NARR,"Imperative and exclamation in reported speech","H","Pair I: when reporting, 'here' normally changes to 'there' ('wait there until he returned'), so leaving 'here' is an error.\nPair II: 'Alas!' becomes 'exclaimed sadly', and 'am' becomes 'was': correct.\nAnswer: (b). Medium confidence: it depends on the setter treating 'here' as an error.")
OW=("Vocabulary","One-word Substitution","One-word Substitution")
