e2(48,D_PAIR+" Identify the pair(s) wherein the one word substitution is correctly stated.","Read the following pairs:\nI. One who knows everything: Omnipotent\nII. One who is all powerful: Omniscient\nIII. One who abandons religious faith: Apostate",["I only","II only","III only","I, II and III"],"C",*OW,"Omniscient versus omnipotent, apostate","E","Omniscient means all-knowing and omnipotent means all-powerful, so I and II are swapped and wrong.\nAn apostate is one who abandons religious faith: III is correct.\nAnswer: (c)")
