e2(49,D_PHR,"The car tended to ______ every time the rains decided to ______.",["act out; come in","act up; come down","act out; come down","act up; come in"],"B",*PV,"Act up and come down","M","Concept: 'act up' means to malfunction; 'come down' describes rain falling heavily.\nAnswer: (b)")
e2(50,D_PHR,"He was eager to ______ after having resigned his position, but was advised to ______ his next move given the prevailing market situation.",["move on; hold on","move off; hold off","move on; hold off","move off; hold on"],"C",*PV,"Move on and hold off","M","Concept: 'move on' means to proceed to something new; 'hold off' means to delay.\nAnswer: (c)")
